{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA380016","title":"Bioflocs metagenome Raw sequence reads","description":"the eel and tilapia waste were used to culture biological floc, to discussion floc nutrient composition and microbial community structure characteristics. Result shew that, group of eel waste as a raw material for floc(A), crude protein was 35.59±0.23%, group of tilapia waste as a raw material for floc(B), crude protein was 29.29±34.95%. Shannon index of group A was 2.15 and group B was 2.37, Group B showed biological floc microbial diversity than group A. At the genus level in group A, total of 135 species of bacteria detection and abundance > 1% of the species has 11, group B detected 128 species, abundance species > 1% has 13.","center":"Shanghai Ocean University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2017/03/21 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN06626971","FlocA.1","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-11-08",2015,"CN","Shanghai",null,null,"unresolved",30.4,120.51,"China:Shanghai","Bioflocs suspended in the tanks farmed eel",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN06626972","FlocA.2","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-11-08",2015,"CN","Shanghai",null,null,"unresolved",30.4,120.51,"China:Shanghai","Bioflocs suspended in the tanks farmed eel",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN06626973","FlocB.1","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-11-08",2015,"CN","Shanghai",null,null,"unresolved",30.4,120.51,"China:Shanghai","Bioflocs suspended in the tanks farmed eel",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN06626974","FlocB.2","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-11-